{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-507", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/507", "wordCount": 961, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hi, my name is Eryk Vershen."}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "I'm an engineer on the HLS"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "Streaming Team."}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "Let's get started talking about"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "HLS Authoring for AirPlay 2"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "Video."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "Ever since we introduced AirPlay"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "on iOS users have enjoyed"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "AirPlaying video to their Apple"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "TVs and starting this year we're"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "expanding that support"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "dramatically with AirPlay built"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "directly into TVs."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "Apple TV and AirPlay capable TVs"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "both provide the highest quality"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "video playback experience."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "You may remember that we have"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "some specific requirements for"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "content delivered to tvOS and"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "Apple TV."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "These AirPlay capable TVs are a"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "new class of devices so they"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "have their own requirements."}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "We have a simple agenda."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "I'll cover the new requirements"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "and then I'll talk about changes"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "we made to the validation tools"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "to help you check for issues."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "We released a new version of the"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "HLS authoring specification"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "recently that talks about the"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "additional requirements for"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "AirPlay 2."}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "Here is a condensed list."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "Don't worry about absorbing this"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "list right now. I'll devote a whole slide to"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "each line item."}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "Let's look at the details."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "You need to synchronize the"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "different variants."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "This makes switching easier."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "If these color bars represent"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "different variants on a"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "timeline, what we want to do is"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "make them all line up nicely."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "We are recommending that you use"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "at least millisecond precision"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "and as always your video"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "segments should start with IDR"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "frames."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "You also want to avoid most"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "changes of discontinuities."}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "For example, do not switch"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "between HEVC and H.264 or"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "between AAC and Dolby Digital."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "These TVs aren't able to switch"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "as seamlessly as iOS or Apple"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "TV."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "You can change your frame rate"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "but not arbitrarily."}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "No switching between 25 frame"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "per second and 30."}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "You also want each codec to"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "provide a good set of variance"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "on its own."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "These TVs will stick with the"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "codec they start with."}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "So, in particular, don't try to"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "use H.264 just for low"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "resolution video and HEVC for"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "high-resolution video."}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "That works on other devices but"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "not here."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "You should, of course, be using"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "I-frame variance."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "They make fast-forward, rewind"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "and seeking more effective."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "Because these devices don't want"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "to switch codecs you need to"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "have a set of I-frame variance"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "matching the codec of the normal"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "video."}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "The encryption requirements"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "listed here aren't really"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "specific to AirPlay 2, but we"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "wanted to call them out."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "The common encryption standard"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "recommends 10% partial"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "encryption."}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "With FairPlay we are requiring"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "it; other patterns will not"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "work."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "For sample encryption there are"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "two ways to market."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "The CMAF way with an senc box"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "and the ISO base media file"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "format way with a pair of saio"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "and saiz boxes."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "We prefer the second form, but"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "you can provide both."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "Lastly, some miscellaneous"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "requirements."}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "If you want to provide HDR"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "content, your best bet is to"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "provide multiple formats."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "For example, Dolby Vision and"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "HDR 10 as TVs may support only"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "one of the formats, use WebVTT"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "for subtitles and we are now"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "recommending MIME types for all"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "your content."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "Let's go into little more detail"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "about that."}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "We've had a MIME type for HLS"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "playlist for a long time."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "The MIME types we are suggesting"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "for video and audio are what you"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "might expect."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "Notice we are using text/plain"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "for WebVTT even though the"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "WebVTT spec says text/VTT."}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "However, the text VTT type was"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "not registered with the IANA and"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "will be rejected by some"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "clients."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "So use text/plain instead."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Here's a list of some of the"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "less common MIME types."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "Now the last 2 on this list are"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "not applicable to AirPlay 2"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "I've listed them because we are"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "recommending MIME types for all"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "content not just AirPlay 2."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "Let's turn to how you can check"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "your streams."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "Remember that there are two"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "tools for HLS validation."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "These tools are complementary."}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "Mediastreamvalidator is checking"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "against the HLS specification."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "HLSreport on the other hand is"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "checking against the authoring"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "specification."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "You should always be using both"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "tools."}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "I suggest you make a script that"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "runs them as a pair."}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "We've made an important change"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "to HLSreport."}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "Formerly you had to run it"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "multiple times with the dash os"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "option if you wanted to check"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "the rules for iOS and TVOS."}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "Now it checks all rule sets by"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "default including the rules for"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "AirPlay 2."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "The rule set option is there to"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "modify the sets you check but"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "most of you won't need to use"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "it. And while the OS option does"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "still work, you should stop"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "using it."}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "Let's look at how the output"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "from HLSreport has changed."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "Notice that the title line now"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "shows all the rule sets that"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "were checked."}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "The rules portion is now grouped"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "into sections for each rule set."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "Here we have the general"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "requirements."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "There can be Must Fix and Should"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "Fix subsections for each rule"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "set."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "Now farther down in the output"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "we have the iOS requirements."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "I want you to notice that rule"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "10 above here the last general"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "rule is marked as Should Fix."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "Whereas here in the AirPlay 2"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "section the same rule is a Must"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "Fix."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "If there are no rule violations"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "for a section or subsection,"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "then that section or subsection"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "is dropped."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "For example, this stream has no"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "Should F ixes for AirPlay 2."}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "The main points to take away are"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "we added new requirements for"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "AirPlay 2 devices."}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "Remember to use HLSreport so you"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "check against the authoring"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "specification."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "And HLSreport now checks all"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "rule sets by default."}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "This is session 507 so you know"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "where to go for more info."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "We'll have links there to the"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "authoring specification to the"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "tools and to other information"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "about HLS."}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "Thanks for your attention."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "Have a great rest of the"}]}
